sentences.l:
First, him, his wife, dear, and his lady mother
tore their hair, onto the well-rolling wagon darting,
laying hold of his head;

And surely all day long until the sinking sun
over Hector, a tear shedding, they would have lamented before the gates,
if the old man out of the chariot had not spoken among the people:

and the child is still an infant, only so,
whom we bore, you and I, ill-fated, nor him do I think
will reach youth;

therefore him the people also lament throughout the town,
and to your parents you made a cursed lament and grief,
Hector;

for not to me, dying, from the bed did you stretch out your hands,
nor did you say to me any solid word, which always
I would remember, nights and days, a tear shedding.”

For other children of mine swift-in-feet Achilles
used to sell, whomever he caught, across the unharvested sea,
to Samos and to Imbros and to Lemnos, misty;

but of you, when he took out the soul with long-pointed bronze,
again and again he dragged you about the tomb of his own companion
Patroclus, whom you slew;

“Hector, to my heart of my husband’s brothers by far dearest of all,
truly my husband is Alexander, godlike in form,
who led me to Troy;

for truly Achilles,
sending me thus, gave charge, from the black ships,
not to do harm before the twelfth dawn comes.”

But when they were gathered and assembled-together had become,
first with fire-faced wine they quenched the pyre throughout
all of it, as far as the might of fire had reached;
